      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi prof, i am having a bit of trouble with phonetics. can u explain the difference between voiced and unvoiced alveolar fricatives? like why is /z/ different from /s/ when they are made in the same place?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hello! Voiced and unvoiced alveolar fricatives differ by the use of vocal cords. For /s/, the vocal cords are held apart, creating a hissing sound (unvoiced). In contrast, for /z/, the vocal cords vibrate, resulting in a buzzing sound (voiced). Despite being produced in the same location by the tongue against the alveolar ridge, the involvement of the vocal cords changes the sound.",
